      "id": 1,
      "text": "Kirkville’s roots trace back to 1794, when the town of Manlius was established alongside Onondaga County’s early formation.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Manlius%2C_New_York",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Erie Canal’s trade boom helped spark Kirkville’s early growth, turning the area into a bustling commercial hub.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Manlius%2C_New_York",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Christ Church and the historic Mycenae Schoolhouse in Kirkville are listed on the National Register of Historic Places.",
